---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Film & Commercial Miniatures | Carve Model"
  description="Miniature sets and physical models for film, commercial, and production teams — built for previsualization, camera planning, and on-location use."
  canonicalPath="/scale-model-services/film"
  ogTitle="Film & Commercial Miniatures | Carve Model"
  ogDescription="Miniature sets and physical models for film, commercial, and production teams — built for previsualization, camera planning, and on-location use."
  active="services"
  imageSlot={true}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={`{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Service","serviceType":"Film & Commercial Miniatures","provider":{"@type":"ProfessionalService","name":"Carve Model","areaServed":["United States","Canada"]}}`} />
<style>
.breadcrumb{padding-top:1.6rem;}
.breadcrumb a{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.78rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);transition:color var(--dur-2);}
.breadcrumb a:hover{color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
.page-hero{padding-top:1.6rem;padding-bottom:clamp(2.5rem,4vw,4rem);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.page-hero h1{margin-top:1.4rem;}
.page-hero p{margin-top:1.4rem;}
.hero__cta{display:flex;gap:0.9rem;flex-wrap:nowrap;margin-top:1.8rem;}
@media(max-width:560px){.hero__cta{flex-wrap:wrap;}}
.hero__cta .btn--primary,.hero__cta .btn--ghost{background:transparent;color:var(--cm-text-strong);border:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);}
.hero__cta .btn--primary:hover,.hero__cta .btn--ghost:hover{background:var(--cm-accent);color:var(--cm-accent-contrast);border-color:var(--cm-accent);}
.dedi-media{margin-top:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);}
.dedi-media image-slot{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:21/9;}
.dedi-body{padding-block:clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem);}
.dedi-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem);align-items:start;}
.dedi-grid h2{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.6vw,2.1rem);letter-spacing:-0.02em;}
.dedi-list{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.4rem 0 0;display:grid;gap:0.8rem;}
.dedi-list li{display:flex;gap:0.7rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:0.98rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
.dedi-list li svg{flex:none;margin-top:4px;color:var(--cm-silver);}
@media(max-width:820px){.dedi-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.svc-section{padding-block:clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-section h2{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.3rem);letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin-top:1rem;}
.svc-section .lead-p{margin-top:1.2rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-checklist{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.8rem 0 0;display:grid;gap:0.75rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-checklist li{display:flex;gap:0.7rem;align-items:flex-start;font-size:0.98rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);}
.svc-checklist li svg{flex:none;margin-top:4px;color:var(--cm-silver);}
.svc-types{display:grid;gap:1.6rem;margin-top:2rem;}
.svc-type{padding-top:1.6rem;border-top:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-type:first-child{padding-top:0;border-top:0;}
.svc-type h3{font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:var(--w-semibold);color:var(--cm-text-strong);letter-spacing:-0.01em;}
.svc-type p{margin-top:0.5rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);font-size:0.95rem;max-width:66ch;}
.svc-steps{display:grid;gap:0;margin-top:2rem;max-width:68ch;}
.svc-step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.4rem 1fr;gap:1rem;padding-block:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.svc-step:last-child{border-bottom:0;}
.svc-step__n{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);padding-top:0.15rem;}
.svc-step p{color:var(--cm-text-muted);font-size:0.95rem;}
.svc-note{margin-top:1.4rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);max-width:68ch;}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main>
<div class="container breadcrumb"><a href="/scale-model-services">← All services</a></div>

<section class="page-hero"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Services / Film &amp; Commercial</span>
  <h1 class="display-lg measure">Physical miniatures built for the shot, the set, or the presentation.</h1>
  <p class="lead measure">Carve Model creates miniature sets and physical models for film, commercial, agency, and creative-production teams.</p>
  <p class="muted measure">Each miniature is developed around how it will be used—whether for previsualization, camera planning, practical filming, a client presentation, a brand activation, or repeated handling during production.</p>
  <div class="hero__cta">
    <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">Get a Preliminary Estimate <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
    <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/works">View Film &amp; Commercial Work <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
  </div>
  <div class="dedi-media"><image-slot id="svc-film-hero" placeholder="Drop film miniature photo" src="/assets/service-product-film-hero-v2.webp"></image-slot></div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Why use a physical miniature?</span>
  <h2>Bring the production into physical space.</h2>
  <p class="lead-p muted">A physical miniature gives directors, production designers, cinematographers, agencies, and clients a shared object they can examine together.</p>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Depending on the project, it can help teams:</p>
  <ul class="svc-checklist">
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Evaluate set composition and spatial relationships</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Explore camera positions and movement</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Plan practical lighting and sightlines</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Communicate an environment before full production</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Develop a complex or inaccessible location</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Create a controllable physical subject for filming</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Present a commercial concept to clients</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Produce a durable display or campaign object</li>
  </ul>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Miniature types</span>
  <h2>Developed around the production requirement.</h2>
  <div class="svc-types">
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Previsualization models</h3><p>Physical planning models used to study composition, blocking, set relationships, camera positions, and production logistics.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Miniature sets</h3><p>Detailed physical environments developed for practical photography or filming. Scale, materials, surface treatment, structure, and access are determined by the intended shots.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Camera and composition studies</h3><p>Models focused on testing viewpoints, lens relationships, framing, sightlines, and movement before committing to a larger set or location.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Commercial product miniatures</h3><p>Reduced, enlarged, or specially constructed product models for advertising, photography, demonstrations, campaign installations, and controlled visual effects.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Presentation models</h3><p>Physical models used by agencies, production designers, and creative teams to explain a set, campaign, environment, or production concept to clients and stakeholders.</p></div>
    <div class="svc-type"><h3>Transportable production models</h3><p>Lightweight, durable models designed for travel, location work, repeated handling, and efficient setup.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Designed for how it will be used</span>
  <h2>The shot determines the build.</h2>
  <p class="lead-p muted">A miniature intended for planning does not require the same construction as one intended for close-up filming.</p>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Before production, we establish:</p>
  <ul class="svc-checklist">
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Intended use and audience</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Camera distance and expected viewpoints</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Required scale and physical dimensions</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Visible and nonvisible areas</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Level of detail required on camera</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Materials and surface treatment</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Structural and handling requirements</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Lighting or practical effects</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Removable walls or access panels</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Transportation and setup requirements</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Production schedule and shooting date</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="svc-note">This helps concentrate effort where it will be visible and useful.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Source material</span>
  <h2>Start with the production information available.</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">We can review:</p>
  <ul class="svc-checklist">
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Production-design drawings</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Art-department sketches</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> CAD and 3D files</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Storyboards and shot references</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Renderings and concept art</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Location photographs</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Product files</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Material and color references</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> AI-generated images</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="svc-note">When no usable geometry exists, Digital Model Development may be separately scoped to translate the approved visual direction into coordinated geometry for fabrication.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Materials and fabrication</span>
  <h2>Balancing appearance, weight, access, and durability.</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Depending on the intended use, a miniature may combine:</p>
  <ul class="svc-checklist">
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Lightweight sheet and foam materials</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Acrylic, ABS, resin, wood, and metal</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> CNC-machined, laser-cut, and 3D-printed components</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Hand-built surface details</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Scenic painting and weathering</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Transparent components</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Integrated lighting</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Removable façades or access panels</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Modular sections</li>
    <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg> Reinforced bases and transport protection</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="svc-note">The material approach is selected according to what the camera or audience will see and how the miniature must perform during production.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Physical and digital communication</span>
  <h2>Complementary tools when the project requires them.</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1rem;max-width:68ch;">Physical miniatures can be coordinated with renderings, animation, AR, VR, or other digital presentation materials when multiple forms of communication would benefit the production.</p>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0.6rem;max-width:68ch;">Carve's core deliverable is the physical miniature. Complementary digital materials are separately scoped according to the project, source information, platform, and intended audience.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="svc-section" style="border-bottom:0;"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
  <h2>A controlled path to production.</h2>
  <div class="svc-steps">
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">01</span><p>Define the production objective and required views</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">02</span><p>Confirm scale, dimensions, access, handling, and transport</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">03</span><p>Review or develop the required geometry</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">04</span><p>Approve materials, finishes, details, and functional features</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">05</span><p>Fabricate and assemble the miniature</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">06</span><p>Finish, inspect, and test required features</p></div>
    <div class="svc-step"><span class="svc-step__n">07</span><p>Package, deliver, and support setup when required</p></div>
  </div>
  <a class="svc-explore" href="/model-making-process" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;margin-top:1.4rem;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.82rem;letter-spacing:0.03em;color:var(--cm-text-strong);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);padding-bottom:2px;">View Our Process <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="cta reveal" style="position:relative;text-align:center;background:var(--cm-black);border:1px solid var(--cm-border);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem) var(--gutter);">
    <h2 class="display-md">Start a film or commercial miniature project.</h2>
    <p class="muted mt-2" style="max-width:52ch;margin-inline:auto;">Tell us how the miniature will be used, what the camera or audience needs to see, and when it is required. Share the production information currently available, and we will recommend an appropriate scope and build approach.</p>
    <div class="hero__cta" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:2.4rem;">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">Get a Preliminary Estimate <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/scale-model-services">All services <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
